    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1323">

                <pb facs="1044" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 151.07/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at
                            Nogales to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The American Consul at Mazatlan telegraphs that the Chinese colony, consisting of
                    four hundred residents, may be compelled to leave Mexico and asks whether
                    permission could be granted for temporary residence, as an act of humanity, at
                    San Francisco or San Diego.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
